name tokmap
category Package
revision 75599
shortdesc Iterate over a token list expandably, without dropping spaces or braced groups
longdesc Usage: \tokmap <command> { <tokens> } applies command over the
longdesc token list tokens. Space tokens, left and right braces are
longdesc replaced with the marker tokens \tokmap@space, \tokmap@bgroup,
longdesc and \tokmap@egroup respectively (which are \ifx-equal to
longdesc themselves exclusively). For convenience, command may contain
longdesc multiple tokens. It is assumed that { and } are the only
longdesc characters with category codes 1 (beginning of group) and 2
longdesc (end of group) respectively. Expandable. This package may be
longdesc used in LaTeX by \usepackage{tokmap}, or in plain TeX and other
longdesc formats by \input{tokmap}. See the visualtoks package for an
longdesc example application.
